# Test images (optional - uncomment if you don't want to commit test images)
# *.jpg
# *.jpeg
# *.png
# *.webp

# Benchmark sample images are auto-generated from corpus.py on first run
# (ground_truth/ JSON is committed -- it's small, human-readable, and useful
# as reference even without regenerating the images)
benchmarks/samples/**/*.png

# Deep Analyze remote bake-off output -- run-specific artifacts (sanitized
# of secrets, but still per-machine/per-run output, not something to check
# in). See docs/REMOTE_BENCHMARK_EXECUTION.md.
benchmarks_remote/results/

# Never commit real provider credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
